      "seq": 2137,
      "acip": ",'DIR SEMS TZAM PAS GAL TE GNYID NANG ZHES SOGS KYIS BSHAD PA BZHIN DU RANG LUGS BZHAG PA LA, SLOB DPON LEGS LDAN GYIS KYANG DPE MA GRUB PA'I LAN MDZAD PA NA, CHOS KYI SKYE MCHED DU GTOGS PA'I GZUGS YID KYI SHES PAS GZUNG BAR BYA BA CIG ,RMI LAM NA YOD PAS RNAM PAR SHES PA NI YUL MED PAR 'GAR YANG YOD PA MA YIN NO ZHES SMRA'O,,",
      "wylie": "'dir sems tsam pas gal te gnyid nang zhes sogs kyis bshad pa bzhin du rang lugs bzhag pa la, slob dpon legs ldan gyis kyang dpe ma grub pa'i lan mdzad pa na, chos kyi skye mched du gtogs pa'i gzugs yid kyi shes pas gzung bar bya ba cig ,rmi lam na yod pas rnam par shes pa ni yul med par 'gar yang yod pa ma yin no zhes smra'o",
      "english": "When those of the Mind Only put forth their own system as expressed in the lines that include “If, in our sleep,” Master Bhavaviveka also responds to it saying that the metaphor doesn't work out; that there is something grasped by the awareness of the thought which is subsumed by the door of sense of all things, and this is present in the dream. As such, as it says, “It is not at all the case that the consciousness here is one for which there is no object.”",
      "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \",'DIR SEMS TZAM PAS GAL TE GNYID NANG ZHES SOGS KYIS BSHAD PA BZHIN DU RANG LUGS BZHAG PA LA, SLOB DPON LEGS LDAN GYIS KYANG DPE MA GRUB PA'I LAN MDZAD PA NA, CHOS KYI SKYE MCHED DU GTOGS PA'I GZUGS YID KYI SHES PAS GZUNG BAR BYA BA CIG ,RMI LAM NA YOD PAS RNAM PAR SHES PA NI YUL MED PAR 'GAR YANG YOD PA MA YIN NO ZHES SMRA'O,,\", \"wylie\": \"'dir sems tsam pas gal te gnyid nang zhes sogs kyis bshad pa bzhin du rang lugs bzhag pa la, slob dpon legs ldan gyis kyang dpe ma grub pa'i lan mdzad pa na, chos kyi skye mched du gtogs pa'i gzugs yid kyi shes pas gzung bar bya ba cig ,rmi lam na yod pas rnam par shes pa ni yul med par 'gar yang yod pa ma yin no zhes smra'o\", \"english\": \"When those of the Mind Only put forth their own system as expressed in the lines that include “If, in our sleep,” Master Bhavaviveka also responds to it saying that the metaphor doesn't work out; that there is something grasped by the awareness of the thought which is subsumed by the door of sense of all things, and this is present in the dream. As such, as it says, “It is not at all the case that the consciousness here is one for which there is no object.”\"}"
